NAME
       mouse_state, keymap_config - input devices

SYNOPSIS
       #include <sys/cervus.h>

       int cervus_mouse_state(cervus_mouse_info_t *out);
       int cervus_keymap_config(int op, const char *arg);

DESCRIPTION
       mouse_state reports the pointer position, the state of the
       left, right and middle buttons, and the accumulated scroll since
       the last call. PS/2 and USB mice feed the same state.

       keymap_config selects the console layouts and the chord that
       switches between them. The layout table is shared by PS/2 and
       USB keyboards, so both behave the same.

RETURN VALUE
       0 on success, negative on failure.

SEE ALSO
       framebuffer(2), csh(1)
